<title>NEW ZEALAND: ANZ cuts NZ 1-yr fixed mortgage rate to 8.95 pct.</title>
<headline>ANZ cuts NZ 1-yr fixed mortgage rate to 8.95 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>ANZ and its partner bank Postbank said on Thursday they would both cut their one-year fixed interest rate for mortgages to 8.95 percent from 9.25 percent. Their variable rate remains at 9.40 percent, to which it was cut on Monday.  </p>
<p>The bank said its move was in response to recent declines in wholesale interest rates.</p>
<p>--Wellington newsroom +64 4 471 4273</p>
</text>
